  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "view-in-github",
        "colab_type": "text"
      },
      "source": [
        "<a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/JoseAlberto88/nlp-mini-projects/blob/main/01_Bidirectional_LSTM.ipynb\" target=\"_parent\"><img src=\"https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg\" alt=\"Open In Colab\"/></a>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# IMDb Sentiment Analysis — Bidirectional LSTM Model\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook builds a Bidirectional LSTM model for sentiment classification using the IMDb dataset.  \n",
        "It follows the architecture demonstrated in the “Natural Language Processing with TensorFlow 2” course, but adapted to our custom preprocessing pipeline created in `00_Text_Preprocessing.ipynb`.\n",
        "\n",
        "### In this notebook, we:\n",
        "- Load the preprocessed dataset (train_ds, val_ds, test_ds)\n",
        "- Create efficient batches for training\n",
        "- Build a Bidirectional LSTM model\n",
        "- Train and evaluate the model\n",
        "- Run predictions on unseen text samples\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook represents the first advanced model in our project.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eLEWRnUtryhg"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Importing the libraries\n",
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "from tensorflow import keras\n",
        "from tensorflow.keras import layers\n",
        "import numpy as np"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xmxCdxxNrzz3"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Loading the IMDb Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "In this step, we load the IMDb movie reviews dataset using `tensorflow_dataset`. The command returns the training set, validation set, a nd test set, already split anf prepared for supervised learning. Ecah element in teh dataset is ap pair: `(text, label)`, where the label indicates sentiment, e.i., `0` for negative and `1` for positiove.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "paFcECgXs3U8"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## Loading the IMDb Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "import tensorflow_datasets as tfds\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load the IMDb dataset with supervised pairs (text, label)\n",
        "\n",
        "(train_ds, val_ds, test_ds), ds_info = tfds.load(\n",
        "    \"imdb_reviews\",\n",
        "    split=[\"train[:80%]\", \"train[80%:]\", \"test\"],\n",
        "    as_supervised=True,\n",
        "    with_info=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Dataset loaded successfully!\")\n",
        "print(ds_info)"
      ],
